[?25l> Done. The translation compiles cleanly. Here's a summary of the key decisions:

- cb_rgb_255 struct uses #[repr(C)] with uppercase field names (R, G, B) matching the C header exactly
- contrast_ratio is extern "C" with #[unsafe(no_mangle)] so it exports with the same symbol name
- The pow() call in C implicitly promotes float args to double (since pow takes double), then the (float) cast truncates back. The Rust translation mirrors this: cast to f64, call .powf(2.4), cast back to f32
- The cbLuminance and cbContrastRatio helpers are private (no pub, no extern "C") since they were static in C
- All arithmetic uses f32 literals (0.2126_f32, 255.0_f32) matching the C float / f suffix semantics✓ Created checkpoint 1



